```

The same pattern repeats for ListFunctions (lines 307-319), Summary (lines 327-340), and Diagnostics (lines 347-359) -- each binding a string and then writing it.

## Estimated savings

~20 lines saved across the 4 query mode branches. Each can be simplified:

```rust
let output = match cli.format {
    Format::Json => writer::write_json_report(&all_cfgs),
    Format::Text => writer::write_text_report(&all_cfgs),
    Format::Dot => writer::write_dot_report(&all_cfgs),
};
write_output(&mut stdout, &output)?;
```

This pattern collapses 9 lines into 5, and applies to all four query modes. Since ListFunctions/Summary/Diagnostics only have Text and Json (with Dot being unreachable), those can still use the same pattern with `Format::Dot => unreachable!()`.

## Current code pattern

In `tests/corpus.rs`, three test functions are nearly identical, differing only in the corpus name and assertion thresholds:

